{"version":1,"slug":"organized__Others__General_Awareness__General_Studies__Super_Practice__General_Awareness_-_General_Studies_-_Super_Practice_-_SSC_SUPER_PRACTICE_41081_(20Q)","path":"organized/Others/General Awareness/General Studies/Super Practice/General Awareness - General Studies - Super Practice - SSC SUPER PRACTICE 41081 (20Q).html","title":"devgagan","provider":"organized","category":"Others/General Awareness/General Studies/Super Practice","durationMinutes":60,"totalQuestions":20,"sectionsLocked":false,"sections":null,"questions":[{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What is malware?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2350;&#2376;&#2354;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">A software developed with good intentions</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2309;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2375; &#2311;&#2352;&#2366;&#2342;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2360;&#2367;&#2340; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2377;&#2347;&#2381;&#2335;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">A software developed to damage hardware and steal data</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2361;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2360;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2361;&#2369;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2337;&#2375;&#2335;&#2366; &#2330;&#2369;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2360;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2377;&#2347;&#2381;&#2335;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">An antivirus program</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2325; &#2319;&#2306;&#2335;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">A firewall protection system</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2347;&#2364;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2357;&#2377;&#2354; &#2360;&#2369;&#2352;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>&#183; Malware (malicious software) is specifically designed to damage computer systems, steal sensitive information, or gain unauthorized access to private networks. </p><p>&#183; It includes viruses, worms, Trojans, ransomware, spyware, and other harmful programs.</p><p>&#183; Unlike legitimate software, malware is created with malicious intent to compromise computer security and user privacy.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following is NOT a type of malware?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2350;&#2376;&#2354;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Virus</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Worm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2368;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Firewall</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2347;&#2364;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2357;&#2377;&#2354;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Ransomware</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2376;&#2306;&#2360;&#2350;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>&#183; A firewall is a security system designed to protect networks from unauthorized access and malicious traffic - it's actually a security tool, not malware.</p><p>&#183; Viruses, worms, and ransomware are all different types of malicious software designed to harm computers or steal data.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What is the main difference between a virus and a worm?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2369;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Virus needs a host program while worm is standalone</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360; &#2325;&#2379; &#2361;&#2379;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350; &#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2340;&#2306;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Virus is more dangerous than worm</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360; &#2325;&#2371;&#2350;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2349;&#2368; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2326;&#2340;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Worm needs a host program while virus is standalone</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; &#2361;&#2379;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360; &#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2340;&#2306;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">There is no difference between them</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2313;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379;&#2312; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>The key distinction is that a virus requires a host program to spread - it attaches itself to legitimate files and spreads when those files are executed or shared. In contrast, a worm is a standalone program that can replicate and spread independently through networks without requiring user action or host files.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>The term 'computer virus' was coined by:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>'&#2325;&#2350;&#2381;&#2346;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2335;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360;' &#2358;&#2348;&#2381;&#2342; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2357;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Alan Turing</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2354;&#2344; &#2335;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2352;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Fred Cohen</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2347;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2337; &#2325;&#2379;&#2361;&#2375;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">John von Neumann</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2332;&#2377;&#2344; &#2357;&#2377;&#2344; &#2344;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2350;&#2376;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Charles Babbage</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2354;&#2381;&#2360; &#2348;&#2376;&#2348;&#2375;&#2332;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Fred Cohen first formally defined and used the term \"computer virus\" in his 1984 paper. While John von Neumann had earlier described self-replicating mathematical automata (a conceptual predecessor), Cohen was the first to specifically define computer viruses as we understand them today and demonstrated the first virus in a controlled laboratory environment.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which malware demands payment to restore access to data?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2350;&#2376;&#2354;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2337;&#2375;&#2335;&#2366; &#2340;&#2325; &#2346;&#2361;&#2369;&#2306;&#2330; &#2348;&#2361;&#2366;&#2354; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Spyware</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Adware</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">ADWARE</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Ransomware</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2376;&#2306;&#2360;&#2350;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Keylogger</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">keylogger</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Ransomware is malware that encrypts a victim's files or locks their system, then demands a ransom payment (often in cryptocurrency) to restore access. Notable examples include WannaCry, Petya, and CryptoLocker. Unlike other types of malware that primarily steal information or damage systems, ransomware's specific business model is extortion through denying access to data.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What is a Trojan?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">A type of antivirus</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2306;&#2335;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">A malware that looks like legitimate software</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2376;&#2354;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2332;&#2379; &#2357;&#2376;&#2343; &#2360;&#2377;&#2347;&#2364;&#2381;&#2335;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2332;&#2376;&#2360;&#2366; &#2342;&#2367;&#2326;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">A network security system</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2375;&#2335;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325; &#2360;&#2369;&#2352;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">A type of firewall</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2347;&#2364;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2357;&#2377;&#2354; &#2325;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>A Trojan (also called Trojan horse) is malware disguised as legitimate software to trick users into installing it. Once installed, it can perform various malicious actions while appearing harmless. The name comes from the Greek story of the Trojan Horse, reflecting how these programs use deception to gain entry to systems.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What is the main purpose of spyware?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2369;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351; &#2313;&#2342;&#2381;&#2342;&#2375;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Display advertisements</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2344; &#2357;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2346;&#2344;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Encrypt user data</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366; &#2337;&#2375;&#2335;&#2366; &#2319;&#2344;&#2381;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2346;&#2381;&#2335; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Gather information without user knowledge</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2367;&#2344;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Generate revenue through clicks</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2381;&#2354;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2350; &#2360;&#2375; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2360;&#2381;&#2357; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Spyware is designed to secretly gather information from a device without the user's knowledge or consent. It can monitor browsing habits, collect login credentials, record personal information, track keystrokes, and transmit this data to third parties. Unlike ransomware or viruses, spyware typically tries to remain undetected to collect information over extended periods.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What security control is primarily designed to prevent malicious code from executing by verifying that programs have not been tampered with? </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2360;&#2369;&#2352;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2306;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2339; &#2350;&#2369;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2342;&#2369;&#2352;&#2381;&#2349;&#2366;&#2357;&#2344;&#2366;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2325;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2352;&#2379;&#2325;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2337;&#2367;&#2332;&#2364;&#2366;&#2311;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2351;&#2361; &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2346;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2331;&#2375;&#2337;&#2364;&#2331;&#2366;&#2337;&#2364; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Antivirus software</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2319;&#2306;&#2335;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360; &#2360;&#2377;&#2347;&#2381;&#2335;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Code signing</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2361;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2352;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Data Loss Prevention (DLP)</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2337;&#2375;&#2335;&#2366; &#2361;&#2366;&#2344;&#2367; &#2352;&#2379;&#2325;&#2341;&#2366;&#2350; (&#2337;&#2368;&#2319;&#2354;&#2346;&#2368;)</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Network Access Control (NAC)</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2344;&#2375;&#2335;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325; &#2319;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2375;&#2360; &#2325;&#2306;&#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2354; (NAC)</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Code signing is a security mechanism that uses digital signatures to verify the authenticity and integrity of software code. It ensures that the code hasn't been altered or tampered with since it was signed by the developer. </p><p>Antivirus software detects and removes malware. </p><p>Data Loss Prevention systems monitor and control data transfers to prevent unauthorized sharing. </p><p>Network Access Control manages which devices can connect to a network.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What is the main purpose of adware?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2337;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2369;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351; &#2313;&#2342;&#2381;&#2342;&#2375;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">To steal data</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2337;&#2375;&#2335;&#2366; &#2330;&#2369;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">To generate revenue through advertisements</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2357;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2346;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2350; &#2360;&#2375; &#2352;&#2366;&#2332;&#2360;&#2381;&#2357; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2346;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">To encrypt files</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2347;&#2364;&#2366;&#2311;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2344;&#2381;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2346;&#2381;&#2335; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">To record keystrokes</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2369;&#2306;&#2332;&#2368;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2377;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Adware is software that automatically displays or downloads advertisements when a program is running or while browsing the internet. Its primary purpose is generating revenue for its creators through advertising. While some adware is legitimate (though annoying), more malicious variants can track user behavior without consent or serve as delivery mechanisms for other malware.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of these is a well-known ransomware?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2311;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2360;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343; &#2352;&#2376;&#2344;&#2360;&#2350;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">WannaCry</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2352;&#2379;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2370;&#2306;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Firefox</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2347;&#2364;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2347;&#2364;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Chrome</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2350;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Safari</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2347;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>WannaCry was a devastating ransomware attack that spread globally in May 2017, affecting over 200,000 computers across 150 countries. It exploited a Windows vulnerability, encrypted files, and demanded Bitcoin payments for decryption. The other options (Firefox, Chrome, and Safari) are legitimate web browsers, not malware.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>What is the recommended frequency for changing passwords according to Clifford Stoll?</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2325;&#2381;&#2354;&#2367;&#2347;&#2379;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337; &#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2377;&#2354; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2360;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337; &#2348;&#2342;&#2354;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2368; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2358;&#2306;&#2360;&#2367;&#2340; &#2310;&#2357;&#2371;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Every month</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2350;&#2366;&#2361;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Every year</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Every six months</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2361;&#2352; &#2331;&#2361; &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Every two years</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2361;&#2352; &#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2366;&#2354; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Clifford Stoll, a notable astronomer and computer security expert, recommended changing passwords every six months as a security best practice. This balance aims to minimize vulnerability while maintaining reasonable usability. However, modern security guidance has evolved, with NIST now recommending password changes only when there's evidence of compromise rather than fixed time intervals.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Select which of the given statement(s) is/are True or False for Direct Action Viruses in computer systems.</p><p>(i) Direct action viruses remain resident in memory after execution and continue to infect files until the system is shut down. </p><p>(ii) Direct action viruses activate immediately when executed and typically target specific file types in the current directory.</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2335;&#2352; &#2360;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2350; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2337;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2375;&#2325;&#2381;&#2335; &#2319;&#2325;&#2381;&#2358;&#2344; &#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2354;&#2340; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2366; &#2330;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p><p>(i) &#2337;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2375;&#2325;&#2381;&#2335; &#2319;&#2325;&#2381;&#2358;&#2344; &#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360; &#2344;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2350;&#2375;&#2350;&#2379;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2344;&#2375; &#2352;&#2361;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2350; &#2348;&#2306;&#2342; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2340;&#2325; &#2347;&#2364;&#2366;&#2311;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2352;&#2326;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;</p><p>(ii) &#2337;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2375;&#2325;&#2381;&#2335; &#2319;&#2325;&#2381;&#2358;&#2344; &#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360; &#2344;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2340;&#2369;&#2352;&#2306;&#2340; &#2360;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2310;&#2350; &#2340;&#2380;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2342;&#2375;&#2358;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2358;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2335; &#2347;&#2364;&#2366;&#2311;&#2354; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2354;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404;</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">(i) True, (ii) True</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">(i) &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;, (ii) &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">(i) False, (ii) True</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">(i) &#2309;&#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;, (ii) &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">(i) True, (ii) False</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">(i) &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;, (ii) &#2309;&#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">(i) False, (ii) False</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">(i) &#2309;&#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;, (ii) &#2309;&#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Statement (i) is false because direct action viruses do not remain resident in memory - they activate, perform their malicious action, and then terminate without establishing persistence. </p><p>Statement (ii) is true as direct action viruses execute immediately when their carrier file is opened and typically target specific files (often .COM or .EXE files) in the current directory before terminating.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Consider the following statements about malware distribution:</p><p>I. Malware can be downloaded from the Internet</p><p>II. Spam emails are a common distribution channel</p><p>III. Network propagation is impossible for malware</p><p>IV. Removable storage devices cannot spread malware</p><p>Choose the correct answer:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2350;&#2376;&#2354;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2340;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;:</p><p>I. &#2350;&#2376;&#2354;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2311;&#2306;&#2335;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375;&#2335; &#2360;&#2375; &#2337;&#2366;&#2313;&#2344;&#2354;&#2379;&#2337; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;</p><p>II. &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2376;&#2350; &#2312;&#2350;&#2375;&#2354; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2357;&#2367;&#2340;&#2352;&#2339; &#2330;&#2376;&#2344;&#2354; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;</p><p>III. &#2350;&#2376;&#2354;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2344;&#2375;&#2335;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2360;&#2366;&#2352; &#2309;&#2360;&#2306;&#2349;&#2357; &#2361;&#2376;</p><p>IV. &#2361;&#2335;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2379;&#2352;&#2375;&#2332; &#2337;&#2367;&#2357;&#2366;&#2311;&#2360; &#2350;&#2376;&#2354;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2347;&#2376;&#2354;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;</p><p>&#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375;&#2306;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">I and II only</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I &#2324;&#2352; II</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">II and III only</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; II &#2324;&#2352; III</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">I, II and III only</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I, II &#2319;&#2357;&#2306; III</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">I and II and IV only</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I, II &#2324;&#2352; IV</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Statements I and II are correct. Malware can be downloaded from the internet (often through deceptive links or compromised websites) and spam emails are indeed a common distribution method. Statement III is false because many types of malware specifically propagate through networks (like worms). Statement IV is false because USB drives and other removable media have been common malware vectors (like the Stuxnet worm).</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Match List I with List II:</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>List I (Malware Type)</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>List II (Characteristic)</b></td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">A. Virus</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">i. Demands ransom</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">B. Worm</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">ii. Needs host program</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">C. Ransomware</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">iii. Standalone program</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">D. Spyware</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">iv. Collects user information</td></tr></table><p>Choose the correct match:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2360;&#2370;&#2330;&#2368; I &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2370;&#2330;&#2368; II &#2360;&#2375; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2319;&#2306;:</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2360;&#2370;&#2330;&#2368; I (&#2350;&#2376;&#2354;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;)</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2360;&#2370;&#2330;&#2368; II (&#2357;&#2367;&#2358;&#2375;&#2359;&#2340;&#2366;)</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">A. &#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">i. &#2347;&#2367;&#2352;&#2380;&#2340;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2306;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">B. &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">ii. &#2361;&#2379;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">C. &#2352;&#2376;&#2344;&#2360;&#2350;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">iii. &#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2337;&#2309;&#2354;&#2379;&#2344; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">D. &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">iv. &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;</td></tr></table><p>&#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2344; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375;&#2306;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">A-ii, B-iii, C-i, D-iv</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">A-ii, B-iii, C-i, D-iv</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">A-iii, B-ii, C-i, D-iv</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">A-iii, B-ii, C-i, D-iv</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">A-ii, B-i, C-iii, D-iv</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">A-ii, B-i, C-iii, D-iv</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">A-iv, B-iii, C-ii, D-i</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">A-iv, B-iii, C-ii, D-i</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>&#183; Virus - Needs host program (viruses cannot execute independently) </p><p>&#183; Worm - Standalone program (worms self-replicate without host files) </p><p>&#183; Ransomware - Demands ransom (defining characteristic) </p><p>&#183; Spyware - Collects user information (primary purpose)</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which of the following statements about virus behavior is correct?</p><p>I. Viruses can steal passwords</p><p>II. Viruses can corrupt files</p><p>III. Viruses can spam email contacts</p><p>IV. Viruses remain active all the time</p><p>Choose the correct answer:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2361;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;?</p><p>I. &#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337; &#2330;&#2369;&#2352;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;</p><p>II. &#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360; &#2347;&#2364;&#2366;&#2311;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2359;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;</p><p>III. &#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360; &#2312;&#2350;&#2375;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2346;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2376;&#2350; &#2325;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;</p><p>IV. &#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360; &#2361;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2360;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351; &#2352;&#2361;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;</p><p>&#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375;&#2306;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">I, II and III only</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I, II &#2319;&#2357;&#2306; III</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">II and III only</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; II &#2324;&#2352; III</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">I and IV only</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I &#2324;&#2352; IV</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">All of the above</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2314;&#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":0,"solution":"<p>Statements I, II, and III are correct. Viruses can steal passwords through various methods, corrupt files (a common virus payload), and spam email contacts (a distribution technique). Statement IV is incorrect because viruses don't necessarily remain active all the time - many are designed to activate under specific conditions or lie dormant to avoid detection.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Consider these statements about antivirus software:</p><p>I. It was initially developed to detect only viruses</p><p>II. It now combats various types of malware</p><p>III. Regular updates are not necessary</p><p>Choose the correct answer:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2319;&#2306;&#2335;&#2368;&#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360; &#2360;&#2377;&#2347;&#2364;&#2381;&#2335;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2311;&#2344; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;:</p><p>I. &#2311;&#2360;&#2375; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; &#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2340;&#2366; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2360;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;</p><p>II. &#2351;&#2361; &#2309;&#2348; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2376;&#2354;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2348;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;</p><p>III. &#2344;&#2367;&#2351;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2346;&#2337;&#2375;&#2335; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;</p><p>&#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375;&#2306;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">I only</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">I and II only</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I &#2324;&#2352; II</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">II and III only</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; II &#2324;&#2352; III</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">All of the above</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2314;&#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Statements I and II are correct. Early antivirus software primarily targeted computer viruses (hence the name), but modern security suites now combat various types of malware including worms, Trojans, ransomware, etc. Statement III is incorrect because regular updates are essential for antivirus software to recognize new malware signatures and threats.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Match the following malware with their primary functions:</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>List I (Malware Type)</b></td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\"><b>List II (Primary functions)</b></td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">A. Keylogger</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">i. Displays advertisements</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">B. Adware</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">ii. Records keystrokes</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">C. Spyware</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">iii. Tracks internet usage</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">D. Trojan</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">iv. Disguises as legitimate software</td></tr></table><p>Select the correct code: </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2376;&#2354;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2341;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2319;&#2306;:</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2360;&#2370;&#2330;&#2368; I (&#2350;&#2376;&#2354;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352;)</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2360;&#2370;&#2330;&#2368; II (&#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2341;&#2350;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351;)</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">A. &#2325;&#2368;&#2354;&#2377;&#2327;&#2352;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">i. &#2357;&#2367;&#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2346;&#2344; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">B. &#2319;&#2337;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">ii. &#2325;&#2368;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2377;&#2352;&#2381;&#2337; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">C. &#2360;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">iii. &#2311;&#2306;&#2335;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375;&#2335; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2379; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2376;&#2325; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">D. &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2332;&#2344;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">iv. &#2357;&#2376;&#2343; &#2360;&#2377;&#2347;&#2364;&#2381;&#2335;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2330;&#2381;&#2331;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;</td></tr></table><p>&#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379;&#2337; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375;&#2306;: </p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">A-i, B-ii, C-iii, D-iv</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">A-i, B-ii, C-iii, D-iv</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">A-ii, B-i, C-iv, D-iii</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">A-ii, B-i, C-iv, D-iii</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">A-iii, B-iv, C-i, D-ii</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">A-iii, B-iv, C-i, D-ii</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">A-ii, B-i, C-iii, D-iv</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">A-ii, B-i, C-iii, D-iv</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>&#183; Keylogger - Records keystrokes (primary purpose) </p><p>&#183; Adware - Displays advertisements (primary function) </p><p>&#183; Spyware - Tracks internet usage (part of information gathering) </p><p>&#183; Trojan - Disguises as legitimate software (defining characteristic)</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Identify the correct statements about malware:</p><p>I. All malware needs a host program</p><p>II. Some malware can replicate on its own</p><p>III. All malware encrypts data</p><p>IV. Some malware can spread through networks</p><p>Choose the correct answer:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2350;&#2376;&#2354;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2361;&#2330;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;:</p><p>I. &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2350;&#2376;&#2354;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2361;&#2379;&#2360;&#2381;&#2335; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;</p><p>II. &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2350;&#2376;&#2354;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2310;&#2346; &#2361;&#2368; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340;&#2367; &#2348;&#2344;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;</p><p>III. &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2350;&#2376;&#2354;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2337;&#2375;&#2335;&#2366; &#2319;&#2344;&#2381;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2346;&#2381;&#2335; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;</p><p>IV. &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2350;&#2376;&#2354;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2344;&#2375;&#2335;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2350; &#2360;&#2375; &#2347;&#2376;&#2354; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;</p><p>&#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375;&#2306;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">I and III only</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I &#2324;&#2352; III</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">II and IV only</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; II &#2324;&#2352; IV</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">I, II and IV only</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I, II &#2319;&#2357;&#2306; IV</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">All of the above</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2314;&#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>Statements II and IV are correct. Some malware (like worms) can replicate independently, and many types can spread through networks. Statement I is incorrect because not all malware needs a host program (worms are standalone). Statement III is incorrect because only specific types like ransomware encrypt data - many other malware types have different functions.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Consider these symptoms of malware infection:</p><p>I. Frequent pop-up windows</p><p>II. Changes to default homepage</p><p>III. Slow computer performance</p><p>IV. Programs starting automatically</p><p>Select the correct answer:</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2350;&#2376;&#2354;&#2357;&#2375;&#2351;&#2352; &#2360;&#2306;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2339; &#2325;&#2375; &#2311;&#2344; &#2354;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;:</p><p>I. &#2348;&#2366;&#2352;-&#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2377;&#2346;-&#2309;&#2346; &#2357;&#2367;&#2306;&#2337;&#2379;</p><p>II. &#2337;&#2367;&#2347;&#2364;&#2377;&#2354;&#2381;&#2335; &#2361;&#2379;&#2350;&#2346;&#2375;&#2332; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2342;&#2354;&#2366;&#2357;</p><p>III. &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2381;&#2351;&#2370;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2343;&#2368;&#2350;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2344;</p><p>IV. &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2310;&#2346; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2366;</p><p>&#2360;&#2361;&#2368; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2330;&#2369;&#2344;&#2375;&#2306;:</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">I and II only</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I &#2324;&#2352; II</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">III and IV only</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; III &#2324;&#2352; IV</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">I, II and III only</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I, II &#2319;&#2357;&#2306; III</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">All of the above</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2314;&#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368;</span>"],"correct_option_id":3,"solution":"<p>All four symptoms are valid indicators of possible malware infection. Frequent pop-up windows (often from adware), changes to default homepage (browser hijackers), slow computer performance (malware consuming resources), and programs starting automatically (malware establishing persistence) are all common signs that a system may be compromised.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>Which type of virus attaches itself to legitimate program files and activates when the infected program is executed? </p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2325;&#2367;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360; &#2357;&#2376;&#2343; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2347;&#2366;&#2311;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2332;&#2369;&#2337;&#2364; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2306;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2346;&#2366;&#2342;&#2367;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Polymorphic Virus</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2346;&#2377;&#2354;&#2368;&#2350;&#2377;&#2352;&#2381;&#2347;&#2367;&#2325; &#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">File Infector Virus</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2347;&#2364;&#2366;&#2311;&#2354; &#2311;&#2306;&#2347;&#2375;&#2325;&#2381;&#2335;&#2352; &#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Multipartite Virus</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2350;&#2354;&#2381;&#2335;&#2368;&#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335;&#2366;&#2311;&#2335; &#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Stealth Virus</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2327;&#2369;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2357;&#2366;&#2351;&#2352;&#2360;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>File infector viruses attach themselves to executable program files (like .EXE or .COM files) and are activated when the host program is run. They can infect other executable files when the infected program is executed. </p><p>Polymorphic viruses change their code to avoid detection. </p><p>Multipartite viruses infect both boot sectors and program files. </p><p>Stealth viruses use various techniques to hide from antivirus programs.</p>","marks":2,"section":null}]}